lse,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-03-23T13:04:51Z","updated_at":"2026-03-30T22:34:28Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.6\n\n### System information\n\nW10\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen you assign a new Resource to some node, the debugger sends this change to the running project. If it's a new resource, instead of assigning it, you will get an error about \"Resource file not found\". While the error is right, I'd rather expect the resource to be properly synced. The problem is that at this point the resource only exists in editor's memory, so the debugger would need to somehow inform the remote project that a new resource was created.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add Sprite2D\n2. Run the project\n3. In the new Sprite2D (local), create a GradientTexture2D in the `texture` property\n4. See errors\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117753/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117753/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}